From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Cap every process's thread pool on Windows

At most 4 foreground and 2 utility workers in every process (the
background pool already has 2). The browser asked for 16 and a
renderer for the CPU count less one; under Playport every thread holds
about 65 MB of FEX's 16 GiB host band (PLA-384). No switch sizes
these pools.
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-trim.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 base/task/thread_pool/thread_pool_impl.cc |   11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/base/task/thread_pool/thread_pool_impl.cc b/base/task/thread_pool/thread_pool_impl.cc
index 02844d94f9..abe3a6111f 100644
--- a/base/task/thread_pool/thread_pool_impl.cc
+++ b/base/task/thread_pool/thread_pool_impl.cc
@@ -55,6 +55,13 @@ enum ThreadGroupType { FOREGROUND = 0, UTILITY, BACKGROUND };
 
 constexpr size_t kMaxBestEffortTasks = 2;
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+// Every process's pools are capped on Windows, for an embedder that must fit
+// several processes' threads in a small address space.
+constexpr size_t kMaxForegroundThreadsOnWin = 4;
+constexpr size_t kMaxUtilityThreadsOnWin = 2;
+#endif
+
 // Indicates whether BEST_EFFORT tasks are disabled by a command line switch.
 bool HasDisableBestEffortTasksSwitch() {
   // The CommandLine might not be initialized if ThreadPool is initialized in a
@@ -193,6 +200,10 @@ void ThreadPoolImpl::Start(const ThreadPoolInstance::InitParams& init_params,
 
   size_t foreground_threads = init_params.max_num_foreground_threads;
   size_t utility_threads = init_params.max_num_utility_threads;
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+  foreground_threads = std::min(foreground_threads, kMaxForegroundThreadsOnWin);
+  utility_threads = std::min(utility_threads, kMaxUtilityThreadsOnWin);
+#endif
 
   // On platforms that can't use the background thread priority, best-effort
   // tasks run in foreground pools. A cap is set on the number of best-effort
